# 7. Data Model

Use the following TypeScript interfaces as the starting contract.

## 7.1 Event

```typescript
interface Event {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  description?: string;
  eventDate?: string;
  currency: string;
  budgetAmount?: number;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

`currency` contains an ISO 4217 currency code.

`budgetAmount` is stored in minor units.

## 7.2 Expense

```typescript
interface Expense {
  id: string;
  eventId: string;
  name: string;
  category?: string;
  expectedAmount: number;
  vendor?: string;
  dueDate?: string;
  notes?: string;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

`expectedAmount` is stored in minor units.

The event determines the expense currency.

## 7.3 Payment

```typescript
type PaymentMethod =
  | "cash"
  | "upi"
  | "bank_transfer"
  | "card"
  | "cheque"
  | "other";

interface Payment {
  id: string;
  expenseId: string;
  amount: number;
  paymentDate: string;
  method?: PaymentMethod;
  notes?: string;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## 7.4 Derived Expense Summary

This is a calculated view model, not a database entity.

```typescript
type PaymentStatus =
  | "unpaid"
  | "partial"
  | "paid"
  | "overpaid";

interface ExpenseSummary {
  expected: number;
  paid: number;
  pending: number;
  overpaid: number;
  status: PaymentStatus;
  progress: number;
}
```

## 7.5 Derived Event Summary

```typescript
interface EventSummary {
  committed: number;
  paid: number;
  pending: number;
  overpaid: number;
  budgetRemaining?: number;
  paymentProgress: number;
}
```

All amounts in these summaries use the event's currency minor units.

