# 16. Error Handling and Data Safety

Implement centralized error handling where appropriate.

Important cases:

| Error | Expected behavior |
|---|---|
| Database unavailable | Show storage error |
| Database write failure | Show failure, preserve existing data |
| Invalid monetary value | Display field validation |
| Invalid payment date | Display field validation |
| Missing event | Show not-found state |
| Missing expense | Show not-found state |
| PDF generation failure | Show error notification |
| Invalid backup | Reject import with details |
| Storage quota exceeded | Warn user |
| Import transaction failure | Roll back changes |

### Destructive Operations

Deleting an event must require confirmation.

Explain that deleting an event also deletes all its expenses and payments.

Deleting an expense must explain that associated payment records will also be deleted.

Payment deletion must require confirmation.

Cancellation and deletion must not be treated as equivalent operations.

Do not silently discard user data.

