# 17. Security and Privacy

The application is intended to operate completely on the client.

Requirements:

- No backend.
- No authentication.
- No remote database.
- No third-party analytics.
- No tracking scripts.
- No unnecessary external network requests.
- No financial data sent to external services.
- Validate imported JSON.
- Render user-provided text safely.
- Avoid unsafe HTML rendering.
- Do not expose database contents in logs.

The application should clearly communicate that clearing browser data may permanently remove locally stored information unless the user has a backup.

